.TH geectl 1  "geectl 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl \- Geeko Controller — a CLI for openSUSE packaging workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\-body\fR] [\fB\-\-live\fR] [\fB\-\-instance\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Geeko Controller — a CLI for openSUSE packaging workflows
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format for the result payload. Applies to every command. Default: the `GEECTL_FORMAT` environment variable, else the `format` key in the config file, else `json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
text
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable the debug channel: human\-readable diagnostic lines on stderr (HTTP attempts, retries, library decisions). Off by default; `GEECTL_DEBUG=1` enables it without the flag
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\-body\fR
Also print request and response bodies on the debug channel (capped at 2048 bytes, redacted, never headers). Implies `\-\-debug`
.TP
\fB\-\-live\fR
Actually perform mutations. Without it, only the plan is printed: dry\-run is the default for mutations
.TP
\fB\-\-instance\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
Select the instance for this call, by its alias in the config file\*(Aqs `[instances]` table. The flag is authoritative: it beats the `GEECTL_OBS_URL` environment variable, the configured URL, and any working\-copy state. For OBS, the flagged alias\*(Aqs URL replaces the configured URL and credentials resolve only from the flagged instance\*(Aqs own variables (`GEECTL_OBS_USERNAME_<ALIAS>` / `GEECTL_OBS_PASSWORD[_FILE]_<ALIAS>` / `GEECTL_OBS_APIKEY[_FILE]_<ALIAS>`); another instance\*(Aqs variables are never borrowed, and a missing credential for the flagged instance fails the call. For Gitea, the host is unaffected, but every Gitea call authenticates with the flagged alias\*(Aqs `GEECTL_GITEA_TOKEN[_FILE]_<ALIAS>` only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
geectl\-version(1)
Print version information as the result payload
.TP
geectl\-config(1)
Inspect or initialise the config file
.TP
geectl\-remote(1)
Remote reads and mutations: inspect what the distribution holds, and change it
.TP
geectl\-request(1)
Read and act on OBS submit requests, and file new ones
.TP
geectl\-branch(1)
Branch, copy, and link packages
.TP
geectl\-build(1)
Build\-status commands: results, logs, histories, binaries, buildconfig
.TP
geectl\-local\-build(1)
Local builds in the podman build vertical: build a package, run its `_service` services, the precommit gate, `spec\-cleaner`, wipe a build root, prune the cache, manage the daily periodic cleanup, enter the preserved build root, and read the log of the last local build
.TP
geectl\-maintenance(1)
Maintenance operations: maintained\-instances listing and maintenance branching
.TP
geectl\-service(1)
Service reads and trigger: list a package\*(Aqs services, their run state, and trigger a server\-side run
.TP
geectl\-gitea(1)
Gitea operations: repository and branch reads and mutations on the configured instance
.TP
geectl\-pull\-request(1)
Read and act on pull requests: OBS submit requests and Gitea pull requests as one surface
.TP
geectl\-person(1)
Search for a person: the OBS projects naming the login and the Gitea users matching the keyword, as one operation
.TP
geectl\-meta(1)
Set the meta of an OBS project, an OBS package, or a Gitea repository as one operation: the target selects the backend
.TP
geectl\-changelog(1)
Validate and generate `.changes` entries in a package directory, pre\-file
.TP
geectl\-checkout(1)
Check out a package into a git working copy, under the current directory
.TP
geectl\-update(1)
Update the working copy in the current directory to the latest base
.TP
geectl\-status(1)
Show the working copy\*(Aqs state against the base
.TP
geectl\-diff(1)
Show the diff of the worktree and the index against the base, plus the link diff on a linked checkout
.TP
geectl\-add(1)
Stage files for commit
.TP
geectl\-rm(1)
Remove files from the working copy
.TP
geectl\-addremove(1)
Stage new files and worktree deletions
.TP
geectl\-commit(1)
Commit the staged changes
.TP
geectl\-pull(1)
Pull a linked package to the link target\*(Aqs latest revision
.TP
geectl\-resolve(1)
Stage the resolved files and continue a stopped rebase
.TP
geectl\-prjconf(1)
Read, validate and clean a project\*(Aqs prjconf
.TP
geectl\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
